{"id":"u-c38def18-f70c-46a4-9631-d5b835424296","src":"community","title":"RP Female Physique: Full Body 4-Day","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/TIDymp-rp-female-physique-full-body-4-day","desc":"UNDERSTANDING THE TRAINING PHASES:\nThe 1st mesocycle \"Basic Hypertrophy\" has enough volume to get you to grow muscle effectively, but it starts out nice and easy so that you can get the most while doing the least you have to. It gets harder as you go, and by the end it will be a real challenge. But when you’ve finished it, you’ll be that much stronger and that much better at doing sets and sets of each exercise. You’ll need to increase the stimulus in order to continue putting on muscle or sparing it from loss during a fat loss diet, and that’s just where mesocycle 2 comes in.\n\nAfter the 1st mesocycle is done, you’ll move onto the 2nd one “Elevated Volume.” Now that you’re much more used to high numbers of sets, this mesocycle starts with more sets than the 1st, and you’ll be able to kick it into high gear sooner. Just surviving the training will be a fun challenge, so you better be ready to work!\n\nAfter the 2nd mesocycle is complete and you’ve done 10 weeks of training, your body will be quite resistant to muscle growth and we’ll need to pull out all the stops for you to keep progressing. In the 3rd mesocycle \"Metabolite Training\", your reps per set will go up considerably as the weights will be intentionally lighter. In addition, the rest time will shorten to just enough time for you to barely catch your breath. How do you know the metabolites are summing up in your muscles during the training? Because of the high reps and short rests, you’ll literally feel a “burn” in your muscles like you might not have felt before. This is exactly what we want, so if you’re feeling it, you’re on the right track!\n\nWhen you’ve completed the 3rd mesocycle, your physique will have changed for the better. But now, because we threw the kitchen sink at your muscles, your body will be very resistant to any further growth in the short term. So how do we get you growing again? You do the 4th mesocycle: “Resensitization.” The process of getting your muscles ready for growth again requires lower volumes of training, so that’s just what this mesocycle will program for you. The training will be heavier than you’re used to, but it will be fewer sets and way fewer reps. You’ll probably not get any big pumps or see any big changes in your physique during this time, but your body is forgetting the high volume training of the last 15 weeks. The next time you train with high volumes again, your body will be ripe and ready to respond with steady growth!\n\nDELOAD:\nThe purpose of this week is to preserve your muscle gains while dropping your fatigue off and allowing you to have another productive training cycle ahead. The week’s rep goal is usually to do 1/2 reps of the start of the mesocycle you're in. If the reps of week 1 are odd numbers, just err on the side of lower. Not only are the reps lower, but the weights will be lower too. If you choose to skip the deload week or make it harder, that is unlikely to be a good decision for your medium and long term training.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-26T20:31:21.451Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper: Push Focus","Lower: Quads Focus","Upper: Pull Focus","Lower: Glutes/Hams Focus"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Walking Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},